{
  "dom_id": "step-q183783",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Describe the set $S=\\{-5,-10,-20,-40,...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}\\}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n-5,\\,-10,\\,-20,\\,-40,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40}{-20} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS=\\{-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
